  "summary_en": "South Africa's draft National AI Policy, published for public comment until 10 June 2026. It sets a vision, six strategic pillars, new institutions (AI Commission, Ethics Board, Regulatory Authority, Ombudsperson, Safety Institute, insurance superfund) and a risk-based, sector-led approach. Robotics is mentioned only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establishes National AI Commission/Office, AI Ethics Board, AI Regulatory Authority, AI Ombudsperson and National AI Safety Institute",
   "Adopts a risk-based approach inspired by the EU AI Act with strict rules for high-risk uses",
   "Proposes an AI Insurance Superfund modelled on the Road Accident Fund to compensate AI harms",
   "Requires sufficient explainability, algorithmic audits and impact assessments for high-risk and public-sector systems",
   "Staged three-year implementation with sectoral working groups and AI strategies"
  ],
